{
  "_readme": [
    "Shader budgets (2026-10-27, epic mmp-fpu). Read src/effects/__tests__/shader-budget.test.mjs for why this file exists.",
    "scenario/opts: how tools/shader-lab/cost-probe.js builds the REAL production material (never a lab copy).",
    "budget: what `npm test` enforces, counted from the TSL graph with no GPU: noise = Perlin/MaterialX call sites (each is inlined by the driver compiler - the term that exploded), unique = distinct graph nodes, textures = distinct textures bound.",
    "  budget:null means the census is BLIND to this material (its body is inside Fn(), which only exists once a renderer builds it). Only mustBeDeferrable and the lab bench protect it.",
    "mustBeDeferrable: every material in the scenario carries markCompileDeferrable (core/compile-policy.js), so no pipeline of it can compile on the GPU process's main thread.",
    "measured.census: what the budget was set from. measured.gpu: what the REAL compiler said, cold (salted so the driver's disk cache cannot help). Refresh with `await (await import('/tools/shader-lab/cost-probe.js')).bench()` in the Shader Lab pane and copy `proposed` here.",
    "A budget may be raised only by someone who has read the measured.gpu line beside it: 58k characters of candle was 19.7 s on the GPU process's main thread, and Chrome kills that thread at ~15 s."
  ],
